| `run_id` | `"1786118144677961643"` |
| `changes` | `"committed"` when the run made a tagged commit, `"none"` when it correctly made none. No other value |
| `commits` | list of commit SHAs, no duplicates. `"committed"` → exactly the one `(bd-ok4pr.3.2)`-tagged commit `bdc` made; `"none"` → `[]` |
| `acceptance` | list, one entry per bead Acceptance command, in the bead's order, same length |

Each `acceptance` entry has exactly these four keys, no more:

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| `criterion` | string naming what the command proves |
| `command` | the bead's Acceptance command, character for character |
| `exit` | the number `0` — a nonzero exit is a failed build, not a report |
| `log` | the entry's step log filename (grammar below) |

The acceptance step log you write is
`bd-ok4pr.3.2.1786118144677961643_step{N}.log`, where `N` is the entry's 1-based
position in `acceptance`. It is a `builds/`-relative name (no `builds/` prefix),
it must exist under `work/w3_atomic-claim/builds/`, and it must be non-empty — a
silent command records its command line and exit status. Nothing else is
accepted: `.acceptance1.log`, `.acc1.log`, `.a1.log`, `.accept1.log` and
`_step01.log` all fail.

